anomaly before, and it would be a mistake to let one so well known as this be our undoing. Further research into the nature and origin of SCP-173 should therefore be initiated at the earliest opportunity, and continued until the Foundation has discovered how much of a threat it truly poses.</span></p> </blockquote> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3460794&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607199503" alt="Kothardarastrix" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3460794)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" >Kothardarastrix</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-147866-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. As first documented by Dr. Moto, SCP-173 is not completely halted by the presence of cameras because it is able to move in short bursts between frames, creating a claymation-like effect that has been described as &quot;creepy&quot; and &quot;disturbing&quot;.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-147866-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. That is, all poses its original creator could have possibly chosen to sculpt it in.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-147866-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. &quot;unconsciousness and memory loss consistent with dissociative amnesia&quot;</div> </div> 
