					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5129</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Keter</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> Due to the erratic and seemingly random appearances of SCP-5129 containment has so far been unsuccessful and as of writing this all further attempts to capture SCP-5129 have been put on hold until further notice.</p> <p>Containment is mainly focused on covering up the various disappearances the entity is responsible for, as well as monitoring the various locations the entity may appear in. Foundation agents are also embedded in various businesses that are responsible for arranging hunting, camping and hiking in an attempt to keep tabs on people who may fall victim to SCP-5129, as well as the areas the entity may appear.<br /> Foundation personnel are also responsible for recovery of the corpses of SCP-5129 victims and are to feed appropriate cover stories to locals and law enforcement.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5129 is an entity that appears randomly in various parts of the Norwegian wilderness, thought to be its primary hunting grounds. It appears as a humanoid creature roughly 1,8 meters in height and wearing green and black winter clothing, it covers its head with the hood of its jacket and has never been observed without it. Due to SCP-5129 anomalous abilities the only known detail about its face is that it has a warm and friendly smile similar to that of a loved one.</p> <p>The entity appears seemingly at random, mostly in secluded areas of the Norwegian wilderness during the winter season. Whenever it appears it will always make contact with people that are alone or lost in the wilderness, such as hikers, outdoorsmen, hunters and campers. Once contact has been made SCP-5129 will reach out its hand in a friendly manner, the contacted individual will then proceed to take SCP-5129 hand before being led by SCP-5129 further into the wilderness and disappear along with the entity. The individual’s corpse will then reappear in a nearby lake several weeks later having seemingly drowned. The corpse will have no signs of a struggle instead appearing to have died quite peacefully, however upon autopsy it will be discovered that the heart of the individual is missing and that the area where the heart should be located have several burns. So far it is unknown why or how SCP-5129 does this or why it seeks out humans in this way, the current theory is that the entity is hunting for sport and is taking the hearts as some sort of trophy.<br /> There have also on occasion been reports of animal remains displayed in a ritualistic manor near the lake in which the corpses appear. These are suspected to be connected to SCP-5129 but this is still unconfirmed at this time.</p> <p>Several attempts at catching SCP-5129 on camera have been made, but attempts have so far been mostly unsuccessful and costly due to SCP-5129 having some unknown anomalous properties that prevent its face from being remembered or described clearly as well as some psychological effect on whoever attempted to do so.<br /> It will always be impossible to describe or remember SCP-5129 face no matter the format, with the only exception being its smile which will always be described as or compared to the smile of a loved one.<br /> The individual that directly attempted to catch SCP-5129 image will begin to constantly feel cold and start having visual hallucinations of ice and snow around them no matter the circumstanses or temperature, most individuals affected by this will end up accidentally killing themselves in an attempt to warm up. D-class personnel affected by this may request termination should they be deemed unnecessary by one or more level 3 researchers assigned to SCP-5129.</p> <p>SCP-5129 has also demonstrated powerful thermokinesis, easily being able to incinerate or completely freeze a human in mere seconds. This ability has so far only been observed once during the latest and currently final capture attempt as detailed below. It Is seemingly capable of creating large fires and structures of ice in a matter of seconds as well as controlling these effects with great precision.</p> <p><strong>Addendum:</strong> Display of previously unknown thermokinetic abilities.</p> <blockquote> <p>Incident Log C-5129-5</p> <p><strong>Log Date:</strong> 13th January 201█ 11:31:43 hours</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> The following is the fifth and currently final attempt to capture SCP-5129. Attempted capture of SCP-5129 involved using one D-class personnel posing as a camper to lure out the entity, once the entity would appear foundation agents would move in on the entity attempting to subdue and capture it following standard containment protocol. All agents involved in the attempt had previous experiences with both hostile and similarly elusive anomalies.</p> <p>It took 9 days for the entity to appear once it did foundation agents moved in using snowmobiles to quickly close the distance. Once engaged however the entity displayed a previously unseen level of aggression as well as previously unknown thermokinetik abilities. In a matter of minutes, the entity destroyed/disabled the head mounted cameras and engaged foundation agents in combat.</p> <p><strong>Begin log:</strong></p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Team leader what is going on out there?&quot;</p> <p><strong>M. Winslow:</strong> (Unidentified roar)</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Team leader please respond we can’t see anything from our end!&quot;</p> <p><strong>M. Winslow:</strong> &quot;Shit, fall back! Command we need an extraction right now!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;What happened?&quot;</p> <p><strong>M. Winslow:</strong> &quot;The thing shoots fire dammit, it incinerated Jack in a matter of seconds, we need help right now!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Alright, the extraction team will be there in 15 minutes. We didn’t know it had pyrokinetic abilities, also something is wrong with the cameras we can’t see anything.&quot;</p> <p><strong>M. Winslow:</strong> &quot;Goddammit this is a disaster! Command the thing is picking us of one by one and bullets have no effect on it.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Please describe, what do you mean?&quot;</p> <p><strong>M. Winslow:</strong> &quot;I mean that we keep shooting it and its just standing there. Hang on its doing something- Holy crap! The thing just skewered most of us where the hell is the rescue dammit!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Explain&#8230; Team leader explain! Marcus do you hear me please explain what’s going on out there?&quot;<br /> <br /> <strong>End log.</strong></p> <p><strong>Aftermath:</strong> 11 minutes after contact was lost the rescue team arrived at the scene to find most of the capture team killed in various gruesome ways. Whilst most of the agents had been burned beyond recognition there were some who had been impaled on large structures of ice and strung up in an almost ritualistic manner. Those not burned had been impaled and strung up in a circle with their limbs outstretched in various ways by the ice as if praying. The remains of the bullets fired at the entity were later recovered having seemingly frozen and shattered on impact.<br /> Only one survivor was found with his body covered in second- and third-degree burns covering roughly 63 percent of his body. Agent Alex Moore spent several months in recovery and underwent several surgeries before being able to fully describe what had happened. He later confirmed that SCP-XXXX did indeed possess thermokinetic abilities and used them to kill the other agents, he also described how the entity propped him up against a tree and made him watch as it strung up the other agents after having burned him, having seemingly deliberately avoided killing him.<br /> Agent A. Moore's description of events seem to suggest that SCP-5129 kills for some ritualistic purpose and or that it takes some sort of sick pleasure in killing.</p> <p>Until further notice no other attempts to capture SCP-5129 are to be authorized. Additionally further research is to be focused on the entity’s abilities and reasoning.</p> </blockquote> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thogri" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6032629&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607199504" alt="Thogri" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6032629)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thogri" >Thogri</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
