d> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4260">SCP-4260</a></td> <td>An armed Mobile Task Force specializing in the location and termination of civilians accidentally affected by the successful neutralization of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4260">SCP-4260</a>; a member of Amalgamate Force Omicron-45.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Tau-1165</td> <td>Snickelway</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1165">SCP-1165</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▷&nbsp;Show&nbsp;list&nbsp;for&nbsp;'Upsilon'</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">◁&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;list</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-1</td> <td>Born from Flesh and Metal</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/apas">Automated Passive Amnestization System Ver. 17.09</a></td> <td>Assembled to explore evacuated Foundation facilities which both contain Keter-class entities and have experience critical structural damage; summarily destroyed by DRO-0001 barring Dr. Tonya Skyler.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-2</td> <td>Cattlewranglers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-843">SCP-843</a></td> <td>Tasked with searching for and containing more instances of SCP-843-2, cattle composed entirely of an unknown plant matter.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-4</td> <td>Hot Iron Strike</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1186">SCP-1186</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-4</td> <td>Please Don't Touch Me</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1627">SCP-1627</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#upsilon-4">MTF-Upsilon-4</a></td> <td>Sugar Pill</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2559">SCP-2559</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2546">SCP-2546</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3519">SCP-3519</a></td> <td>Originally formed in order to contain SCP-2559, Mobile Task Force Upsilon-4 is tasked with epidemiological containment, especially with the containment of memetic outbreaks.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Upsilon-4</td> <td>[DATA MISSING]</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4848">SCP-4848</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-7</td> <td>The Glass Jar</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2977">SCP-2977</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1077">SCP-1077</a></td> <td>Specializes in the containment (or decommissioning) of biological anomalies under the guise of nature and wildlife preservation.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Upsilon-8</td> <td>Cavity Creeps</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5799">SCP-5799</a></td> <td>Task force that specializes in the containment of dental anomalies. Often composed of dental surgeons or personnel holding a degree of knowledge in the field of dentistry.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Upsilon-11</td> <td>Avalon's Wake</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4793">SCP-4793</a></td> <td>Operating with SCP-4793 and combat against members of the Chaos Insurgency. Specializes in defense against hostiles.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Upsilon-18</td> <td>Black Noise, Digital Millennium Copyright Agents</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2266">SCP-2266</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/eulogy-for-the-living">Eulogy For The Living</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/brotherhood">Brotherhood</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1617">SCP-1617</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task forces.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-20</td> <td>Hogtown Garrison</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2417">SCP-2417</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/wrong-eve">Wrong Eve</a></td> <td>Contains anomalies found in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, and the surrounding areas. Stationed at Site-201.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-23</td> <td>Art Critics</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1226">SCP-1226</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1018">SCP-1018</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3435">SCP-3435</a></td> <td>Specializes in the containment of anart.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-51</td> <td>Red Hand</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2299">SCP-2299</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Upsilon-53</td> <td>Alien Robots In Space</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4011">SCP-4011</a></td> <td>Task force comprised of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1360">PSHUD</a> units, created in mid-2052 to contain SCP-4011. Specializes in operations under environmental conditions which would be fatal to human personnel.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-89</td> <td>Nobodies</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2034">SCP-2034</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-90</td> <td>Andalusian Dogs</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3996">SCP-3996</a></td> <td>Specialises in extradimensional exploration.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-638</td> <td>Phoenix Nest</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1115">SCP-1115</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Upsilon-Peorð</td> <td>Slings and Arrows</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3676">SCP-3676</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4029">SCP-4029</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4377">SCP-4377</a></td> <td>A distributed task force consisting of multiple discrete units, specialising in the non-lethal containment of immense anomalous fauna and pseudo-fauna. The unit assigned to 3676 may contain multiple different iterations of the same personnel.</td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" hr